# Session tag presentation

Tags use the padding before the repository without changing names, attention
pips, agent summaries, or matching text. Create live sessions with different
name lengths and a shared repository. Direct metadata setup gives each session
all 26 tags without 26 CLI process launches per session.

    :b jj cat sh tmux (available)
    :cp tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)
    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :$ -q smth --no-base --create-repo --create alpha (exit: 0)
    :t new-session -d -s medium-name-with-limited-padding "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s name-that-fills-the-entire-forty-columnsxx "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -t medium-name-with-limited-padding @smth.repo alpha (success)
    :t set-option -t name-that-fills-the-entire-forty-columnsxx @smth.repo alpha (success)
    :$ -q sh -c 'for session in alpha medium-name-with-limited-padding name-that-fills-the-entire-forty-columnsxx; do for tag in a b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p q r s t u v w x y z; do tmux set-option -t "=$$session:" "@smth.tag.$$tag" 1; done; done' (exit: 0)
    :t set-option -t alpha @smth.flag 1 (success)
    :t set-option -p -t alpha:0 @smth.agent.state waiting (success)
    :t new-session -d -s ui "smth; cat" (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 100 -y 12 (success)
    :p ui:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :k C-p alpha

The short name leaves enough padding for every tag and an alignment space in
the ellipsis column; the footer repeats full
membership beside the left-aligned controls. Colour is intentional: selected
and unselected tags are bold flag-blue, independent of the attention pip.

    :snap --color

```terminal
session: alpha                                                                                     ┃
  3/5 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                                        ⏸ ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
   alpha~1                                                                                    tmux ┃
▌■ alpha        abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz  ~/alpha                                              ⏸ ┃
 ■ medium-name-with-limited-padding abcdef… alpha                                                  ┃
 ■ name-that-fills-the-entire-forty-columnsxx alpha                                                ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] unflag, [C-t] tags: abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz                                 ┃
```

![light](session-tags.md.snap.1.light.svg)
![dark](session-tags.md.snap.1.dark.svg)

The medium name leaves only a small gap. It remains complete while tags contract
with an ellipsis; the footer shows membership beside its controls when it fits.

    :k C-u medium
    :snap

```terminal
session: medium                                                                                    ┃
  1/5 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                                        ⏸ ┃
   medium                                   ~/medium                                          repo ┃
   medium                                                                                     tmux ┃
▌■ medium-name-with-limited-padding abcdef… alpha                                                  ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] flag, [C-t] tags: abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz                                   ┃
```

The forty-column name leaves no padding, so inline tags disappear entirely.
The footer identifies the tags and the repository follows the full name.

    :k C-u name-that
    :snap

```terminal
session: name-that                                                                                 ┃
  1/5 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                                        ⏸ ┃
   name-that                                ~/name-that                                       repo ┃
   name-that                                                                                  tmux ┃
▌■ name-that-fills-the-entire-forty-columnsxx alpha                                                ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
                                                                                                   ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] flag, [C-t] tags: abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz                                   ┃
```

Narrowing the terminal clips the already constructed rows without recontracting
tags. Horizontal scrolling can clip names to keep repository matches visible;
the medium row retains its name-column-based ellipsis. The footer also stays
one line and clips its contents rather than shrinking the session list.

    :k C-u alpha
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 25 -y 12 (success)
    :snap -d 2s

```terminal
session: alpha          ┃
  3/5 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓ ⏸ ┃
                        ┃
   alpha~1         tmux ┃
▌■ alpha        abcde ⏸ ┃
 ■ padding abcdef… alpha┃
 ■ forty-columnsxx alpha┃
                        ┃
                        ┃
                        ┃
                        ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] unfl┃
```

    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 9 -y 12 (success)
